message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Clean AI Engineering: principles, specification formats and gates for building AI agents as testable software"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
authors:
  - given-names: Basant
    family-names: Choudhary
    affiliation: "DataAgents.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dataagentsai/clean-ai-engineering"
url: "https://github.com/dataagentsai/clean-ai-engineering"
abstract: >-
  The umbrella of a family of open specifications for AI agents: the principles, the Spec Charter that routes each statement to the right specification, the Baseline of software practice cited rather than restated, the draft per-agent specification format (AOAS), and the four gates (behaviour, features, structure, harness) with the cycle that routes every failure back to a specification. It joins the AI Assurance Catalog (what must be true), the AI Harness Catalog (what must exist) and AgentTwin (what an agent must face).
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - AI engineering
  - specification
  - agent evaluation
  - LLM applications
